# Canonical identity for the platform's automation account.
#
# The bot that authors commits from the workstation and CI was renamed from
# "Arlo Bot" to "runink-core". Renaming the identity does not retroactively
# change ~2800 existing commits, and rewriting history to do so would break
# every published SHA. .mailmap is the non-destructive equivalent: git log,
# git shortlog and git blame display the canonical name, while the objects
# stay untouched.
#
# Mapped by NAME AND EMAIL, not email alone, deliberately: one legacy variant
# used paes@runink.org, which is also the humans' address. An email-only rule
# would relabel their commits as the bot.
#
# Note: GitHub's web UI does not honour .mailmap (it attributes by commit
# email), so this normalises local git tooling only.
runink-core <bot@runink.org> Arlo Bot <bot@runink.org>
runink-core <bot@runink.org> Arlo Bot <paes@runink.org>
runink-core <bot@runink.org> Arlo Bot <arlo@dashie.ink>
runink-core <bot@runink.org> Arlobot <arlobot@runink.org>
